), la armonía vocal (Manhattan Transfer, Roches, McGarrigle Sisters) y los cincuenta (American Graffiti).","color":"#f59e0b","family":"Raíces: rock'n'roll, country y roots","link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#country-rock"}],"book_tracks":[{"id":267278115894656,"artist":"Leon Redbone","artist_id":42015324504704,"title":"On The Track","year":1976,"ess":0,"yt":"HZDP42dZHA0","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Country-rock y roots-rock","scene_id":277196802515577,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#country-rock","chapters":["Sección 4.2"],"pages":[[1,81,null]]}],"mentions":[{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":81,"text":"…Coming Out (1976), transformed from novelty act of the nostalgia movement to chamber performers with Extensions (1979). The eccentric and eclectic Leon Redbone, armed with his baritone croon and yodel and his nostalgic orchestrations (heavy on the strings and horns), devoted his career to injecting new life…"}],"podcast":[],"awards":[],"concerts":[],"xref":[],"charts":[{"id":267278115894656,"type":"album","name":"On the Track","list_id":42506770247937,"list":"RYM Top — Jazz — Dixieland","src":"musthear","rank":7,"year":1975,"note":null,"yt":"HZDP42dZHA0","scaruffi":null},{"id":267278115894656,"type":"album","name":"On the Track","list_id":162167649040794,"list":"RYM Top — Musical Theatre and Entertainment","src":"musthear","rank":22,"year":1975,"note":null,"yt":"HZDP42dZHA0","scaruffi":null},{"id":267278115894656,"type":"album","name":"On the Track","list_id":72780663088705,"list":"RYM Top — Musical Theatre and Entertainment — Vaudeville","src":"musthear","rank":4,"year":1975,"note":null,"yt":"HZDP42dZHA0","scaruffi":null},{"id":267278115894656,"type":"album","name":"On the Track","list_id":280702155250789,"list":"RYM Top — Regional Music — Ragtime","src":"musthear","rank"